1
00:00:00,766 --> 00:00:01,199
 Hi!

2
00:00:01,399 --> 00:00:05,233
 In this video I'm going to edit a short
 city film from start to

3
00:00:05,233 --> 00:00:08,566
 finish and I'll do almost all of
 it with the loop deck.

4
00:00:08,933 --> 00:00:12,666
 Along the way you'll see every page
 and every button of the Tika

5
00:00:12,666 --> 00:00:15,033
 Studio's loop deck pack in the order

6
00:00:15,033 --> 00:00:16,933
 you'd actually use them when you edit.

7
00:00:17,233 --> 00:00:20,833
 There's a studio edition for DaVinci
 Resolve Studio and a free

8
00:00:20,833 --> 00:00:22,899
 edition for the free version of DaVinci.

9
00:00:23,066 --> 00:00:24,899
 Everything you see works in both,

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,066
 unless I tell you it's studio only.

11
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:28,733
 And if you still need to install the

12
00:00:28,733 --> 00:00:31,166
 pack, there's a short separate
 video for that.

13
00:00:31,433 --> 00:00:32,866
 The link is in the description.

14
00:00:33,133 --> 00:00:34,633
 First, a quick tour.

15
00:00:34,933 --> 00:00:37,766
 The eight round buttons at the
 bottom are your pages.

16
00:00:37,933 --> 00:00:42,000
 Round button 1, on the bottom left,
 takes you to the media page.

17
00:00:42,166 --> 00:00:44,233
 Button 2 is the edit page.

18
00:00:44,399 --> 00:00:47,000
 Buttons 3 and 4 are edit pages too.

19
00:00:47,299 --> 00:00:50,666
 DaVinci stays where it is, but the
 loop deck gets a new set of

20
00:00:50,666 --> 00:00:54,166
 buttons, so you get three edit
 pages full of tools.

21
00:00:54,366 --> 00:00:58,666
 Button 5 is the color page. 6 is
 Fairlight for your sound.

22
00:00:59,033 --> 00:01:01,799
 And 7 is Deliver, where you
 export your film.

23
00:01:02,033 --> 00:01:05,066
 Button 8, on the bottom right,
 is Quick Export.

24
00:01:05,299 --> 00:01:07,833
 I'll save that one for the end,
 when the film is finished.

25
00:01:08,099 --> 00:01:09,866
 Above the round buttons is the touch

26
00:01:09,866 --> 00:01:13,166
 screen, with 12 buttons that
 change on every page.

27
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:15,933
 On the left and the right
 you have 6 dials.

28
00:01:16,066 --> 00:01:18,066
 You can turn them and you can press them.

29
00:01:18,433 --> 00:01:22,166
 In the middle is the big wheel, and next
 to it, the square buttons.

30
00:01:22,333 --> 00:01:24,099
 I'll show you all of them while we edit.

31
00:01:24,433 --> 00:01:25,133
 Let's go!

32
00:01:29,533 --> 00:01:32,533
 Round button 1 takes me
 to the media page.

33
00:01:32,766 --> 00:01:34,933
 This is where every project starts.

34
00:01:35,266 --> 00:01:38,133
 On the touch screen, the middle
 row, third button.

35
00:01:38,466 --> 00:01:39,633
 Project Settings.

36
00:01:39,799 --> 00:01:42,799
 This is where you choose the size and
 the frame rate of your film.

37
00:01:43,299 --> 00:01:47,433
 I'm making a normal 1080p film
 at 25 frames per second.

38
00:01:47,833 --> 00:01:50,066
 That's already set, so I'll
 just close it.

39
00:01:50,466 --> 00:01:52,366
 Next, I want two folders.

40
00:01:52,533 --> 00:01:54,833
 One for the music, and one
 for the footage.

41
00:01:55,066 --> 00:01:56,666
 Top row, second button.

42
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:57,599
 New bin.

43
00:01:57,966 --> 00:01:59,599
 I'll call this one Music.

44
00:01:59,933 --> 00:02:02,433
 One more press, and this one is footage.

45
00:02:02,866 --> 00:02:03,866
 Now the files.

46
00:02:04,133 --> 00:02:07,566
 I click on the music bin and use the
 first button on the top row.

47
00:02:07,799 --> 00:02:08,800
 Import media.

48
00:02:09,199 --> 00:02:10,033
 There's my song.

49
00:02:10,366 --> 00:02:11,699
 Open, and it's in.

50
00:02:12,066 --> 00:02:14,966
 Then the footage bin, and
 import media again.

51
00:02:15,333 --> 00:02:19,133
 I go to my footage folder, select all
 four clips, and open them.

52
00:02:19,366 --> 00:02:21,400
 Four city clips, ready to edit.

53
00:02:21,766 --> 00:02:23,366
 Bottom row, first button.

54
00:02:23,633 --> 00:02:24,566
 Power bins.

55
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:27,133
 It hides your power bins and
 shows them again.

56
00:02:27,433 --> 00:02:30,500
 Power bins are folders you can
 use in every project.

57
00:02:30,733 --> 00:02:33,233
 Perfect for your logo or your
 favorite titles.

58
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:35,033
 Top row, third button.

59
00:02:35,266 --> 00:02:35,833
 Note.

60
00:02:36,099 --> 00:02:37,766
 These are the notes of your project.

61
00:02:38,033 --> 00:02:39,866
 I'll write a little reminder for myself.

62
00:02:40,066 --> 00:02:42,433
 Cut on the beat, and night
 clips at the end.

63
00:02:42,666 --> 00:02:44,166
 Save it, and close.

64
00:02:44,366 --> 00:02:46,000
 Top row, last button.

65
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:47,233
 Project manager.

66
00:02:47,433 --> 00:02:49,933
 This is where you open or
 switch projects.

67
00:02:50,166 --> 00:02:51,033
 I'll close it again.

68
00:02:51,366 --> 00:02:53,033
 Middle row, last button.

69
00:02:53,233 --> 00:02:54,233
 New project.

70
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,933
 For when you want to start something new.

71
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:57,266
 I'll cancel this one.

72
00:02:57,566 --> 00:02:59,366
 Two buttons are for heavy footage,

73
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:01,099
 and they sit right next to each other.

74
00:03:01,333 --> 00:03:02,900
 Middle row, first button.

75
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:04,300
 Prefer proxy.

76
00:03:04,533 --> 00:03:07,766
 DaVinci now plays your smaller proxy
 files if you made them.

77
00:03:08,033 --> 00:03:09,866
 You can see it up here, in purple.

78
00:03:10,099 --> 00:03:12,599
 And right next to it, camera originals.

79
00:03:12,733 --> 00:03:15,333
 That switches back to your original
 camera files.

80
00:03:15,599 --> 00:03:17,833
 The bottom row has three more buttons.

81
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,866
 Timeline 9x16, 4x5, and 4x3.

82
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:23,666
 They turn your finished timeline

83
00:03:23,666 --> 00:03:25,766
 into a vertical or a square version.

84
00:03:26,133 --> 00:03:29,199
 These are studio only, and they're
 most useful when your film is

85
00:03:29,199 --> 00:03:31,233
 done, so I'll show you those at the end.

86
00:03:31,566 --> 00:03:33,466
 In the free edition, this row has

87
00:03:33,466 --> 00:03:36,099
 duplicate timeline and new
 timeline instead.

88
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:39,400
 One more thing on this page, and
 it's one of my favorites.

89
00:03:39,533 --> 00:03:42,800
 Swipe the touchscreen to the right
 and you get the break timer.

90
00:03:42,966 --> 00:03:44,800
 This one is studio only as well.

91
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:49,599
 I'm going to edit for 25 minutes, so
 I tap 25 minutes and start.

92
00:03:49,833 --> 00:03:51,133
 Look at the status button.

93
00:03:51,366 --> 00:03:53,233
 The timer is really running now.

94
00:03:53,766 --> 00:03:55,766
 2459, 2458.

95
00:03:56,166 --> 00:03:59,099
 Keep an eye on it because it will come
 back later in this video.

96
00:03:59,333 --> 00:04:01,666
 Stop ends the timer if you ever need it.

97
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:04,133
 And this button opens Rushwise, my

98
00:04:04,133 --> 00:04:06,366
 project manager for DaVinci editors.

99
00:04:06,633 --> 00:04:08,199
 Now, let's start editing.

100
00:04:12,566 --> 00:04:15,266
 Round button 2 takes DaVinci to the edit

101
00:04:15,266 --> 00:04:17,899
 page, and the loop deck to edit page 1.

102
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:19,699
 First, I need a timeline.

103
00:04:20,166 --> 00:04:24,433
 That button lives on edit page 3,
 so I tap round button 4.

104
00:04:24,833 --> 00:04:28,366
 DaVinci stays on the edit page, but
 the touchscreen changes.

105
00:04:28,633 --> 00:04:30,266
 Bottom row, second button.

106
00:04:30,533 --> 00:04:31,466
 New timeline.

107
00:04:31,766 --> 00:04:34,266
 I'll call it "City Film" and create it.

108
00:04:34,466 --> 00:04:37,500
 Then back to round button
 2 for edit page 1.

109
00:04:37,866 --> 00:04:41,133
 Putting clips on a timeline is something
 you do with your mouse.

110
00:04:41,366 --> 00:04:44,533
 I select my four clips and drag
 them onto the timeline.

111
00:04:44,866 --> 00:04:46,166
 The film doesn't fit on the

112
00:04:46,166 --> 00:04:48,933
 screen, so I press the middle right dial.

113
00:04:49,166 --> 00:04:50,166
 Zoom to fit.

114
00:04:50,433 --> 00:04:51,933
 Now I can see all of it.

115
00:04:52,233 --> 00:04:55,199
 From the music bin, I drag the
 song in underneath.

116
00:04:55,533 --> 00:04:57,166
 Now let's look at all the ways to

117
00:04:57,166 --> 00:04:59,466
 move through your timeline, in one go.

118
00:04:59,766 --> 00:05:01,600
 I click somewhere in the first clip.

119
00:05:01,866 --> 00:05:04,866
 The big wheel in the middle moves
 you frame by frame.

120
00:05:05,133 --> 00:05:07,266
 Right is forward, left is back.

121
00:05:07,533 --> 00:05:08,866
 Keep an eye on the timecode.

122
00:05:09,166 --> 00:05:11,033
 The top left dial does the same.

123
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:13,399
 That's shuttle, frame by frame.

124
00:05:13,666 --> 00:05:15,933
 The top right dial is fast shuttle.

125
00:05:16,166 --> 00:05:18,000
 Every click is a whole second.

126
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:20,399
 The bottom right dial is next clip.

127
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:22,199
 It jumps from cut to cut.

128
00:05:22,399 --> 00:05:25,100
 And the middle right dial
 zooms in and out.

129
00:05:25,333 --> 00:05:28,100
 On the square buttons, D
 jumps to the end of

130
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:31,033
 your timeline, and C takes you
 back to the start.

131
00:05:31,266 --> 00:05:34,266
 To play, tap the bottom right button
 on the touchscreen.

132
00:05:34,533 --> 00:05:35,766
 Play and pause.

133
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,366
 Tap it again to stop.

134
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:40,533
 It's on every edit page, so you
 never have to switch.

135
00:05:40,733 --> 00:05:42,766
 Or tap the middle of the big wheel.

136
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,466
 Play and pause.

137
00:05:44,733 --> 00:05:46,166
 Now, markers.

138
00:05:46,366 --> 00:05:48,066
 You can put them in two places.

139
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:51,100
 With a clip selected, the markers
 go on the clip.

140
00:05:51,333 --> 00:05:54,533
 I play the song and tap the bottom
 right dial on the beat.

141
00:05:54,766 --> 00:05:56,199
 That's add marker.

142
00:05:56,433 --> 00:05:58,699
 Look, they land right on the first clip.

143
00:05:58,933 --> 00:06:01,766
 With nothing selected, they go
 on the timeline itself.

144
00:06:01,966 --> 00:06:05,600
 One press, and another, and there
 they are, up in the ruler.

145
00:06:07,466 --> 00:06:08,399
 Time to cut.

146
00:06:08,733 --> 00:06:10,733
 I select the first clip and put the

147
00:06:10,733 --> 00:06:12,633
 playhead where I want it to start.

148
00:06:12,866 --> 00:06:13,633
 Touch screen.

149
00:06:13,866 --> 00:06:16,933
 Bottom row, first button, ripple start.

150
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:19,000
 Everything before the playhead is

151
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,533
 gone, and the rest of the
 film moves along.

152
00:06:21,766 --> 00:06:22,533
 No gap.

153
00:06:22,899 --> 00:06:24,866
 Now I put the playhead where
 the clip should

154
00:06:24,899 --> 00:06:27,733
 end, and use the third button
 on the bottom row.

155
00:06:27,966 --> 00:06:28,966
 Ripple end.

156
00:06:29,266 --> 00:06:31,966
 The end is gone, and again, no gap.

157
00:06:32,333 --> 00:06:35,100
 On the second clip, I put the
 playhead in the middle.

158
00:06:35,333 --> 00:06:38,233
 Bottom row, second button, split clip.

159
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:41,166
 It cuts the clip in two, right
 at the playhead.

160
00:06:41,433 --> 00:06:42,766
 I don't need the second half.

161
00:06:43,033 --> 00:06:45,633
 Top row, last button, delete.

162
00:06:45,933 --> 00:06:48,866
 The clip is gone, but this
 time it leaves a gap.

163
00:06:49,133 --> 00:06:50,800
 That's fine, I'll close it later.

164
00:06:51,166 --> 00:06:53,399
 On the third clip, I want
 something different.

165
00:06:53,566 --> 00:06:56,133
 Trim it, but leave everything
 else where it is.

166
00:06:56,366 --> 00:06:59,233
 Middle row, first button, trim start.

167
00:06:59,433 --> 00:07:02,399
 And with the playhead a bit further,
 the button next to it.

168
00:07:02,566 --> 00:07:03,466
 Trim end.

169
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:06,066
 The clip is shorter, and the gaps stay.

170
00:07:06,366 --> 00:07:07,966
 Top row, second button.

171
00:07:08,266 --> 00:07:10,100
 With the playhead here, select

172
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:12,800
 forward all selects everything
 to the right.

173
00:07:13,033 --> 00:07:16,000
 Handy when you want to move the rest
 of your film in one go.

174
00:07:16,233 --> 00:07:19,933
 The first button, select backward all,
 does the same to the left.

175
00:07:20,266 --> 00:07:21,533
 Now, snapping.

176
00:07:21,833 --> 00:07:24,166
 When snapping is on, a clip jumps to

177
00:07:24,166 --> 00:07:26,466
 the edge of the next clip, like a magnet.

178
00:07:26,766 --> 00:07:30,033
 I drag the last clip to the left,
 and it clicks into place.

179
00:07:30,233 --> 00:07:32,899
 Snapping is the third button
 on the top row.

180
00:07:33,133 --> 00:07:34,866
 I turn it off, and now I can put a

181
00:07:34,866 --> 00:07:37,800
 clip anywhere I want, even
 one frame away.

182
00:07:38,133 --> 00:07:40,566
 I'll undo that, and switch
 snapping back on.

183
00:07:42,566 --> 00:07:46,466
 The last clip is a night time lapse,
 and it can go faster.

184
00:07:46,833 --> 00:07:50,166
 I select it, and on the middle
 row, the last button.

185
00:07:50,466 --> 00:07:54,233
 Change clip speed. 200% and change.

186
00:07:54,533 --> 00:07:56,766
 Twice as fast, and half as long.

187
00:07:57,199 --> 00:07:59,033
 The button next to it, retime

188
00:07:59,033 --> 00:08:01,866
 controls, shows the speed
 right on the clip.

189
00:08:02,133 --> 00:08:03,600
 Tap it again to hide it.

190
00:08:03,899 --> 00:08:05,899
 You can also press the dials, and

191
00:08:05,899 --> 00:08:07,533
 then they give your clips a color.

192
00:08:07,833 --> 00:08:09,733
 Great to keep your timeline organized.

193
00:08:09,966 --> 00:08:12,966
 The first clip, top left dial, orange.

194
00:08:13,199 --> 00:08:16,199
 The second clip, middle
 left dial, yellow.

195
00:08:16,466 --> 00:08:19,333
 The third clip, top right dial, green.

196
00:08:19,733 --> 00:08:21,199
 Now I select the music.

197
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,166
 Turn the middle left dial, and

198
00:08:23,199 --> 00:08:25,766
 every click makes it one decibel softer.

199
00:08:26,033 --> 00:08:28,366
 Six clicks, six decibels down.

200
00:08:28,733 --> 00:08:31,066
 The bottom left dial is dynamic trim.

201
00:08:31,333 --> 00:08:33,899
 Put the playhead on a cut,
 press the dial to

202
00:08:33,899 --> 00:08:36,600
 switch dynamic trim on, and
 select the cut.

203
00:08:36,966 --> 00:08:40,600
 Now turn the dial, and the cut
 moves, frame by frame.

204
00:08:40,933 --> 00:08:43,233
 In the viewer, you see both
 sides of the cut.

205
00:08:43,533 --> 00:08:45,600
 Press the dial again to switch it off.

206
00:08:49,833 --> 00:08:53,466
 Round button 3 switches the loop
 deck to edit page 2.

207
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,133
 The markers I made aren't needed anymore.

208
00:08:56,566 --> 00:08:59,133
 Top left, delete all markers.

209
00:08:59,366 --> 00:08:59,766
 Gone.

210
00:09:00,266 --> 00:09:01,933
 The second button is link.

211
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:04,733
 It switches linked selection on and off.

212
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:07,166
 I switch it off, and now a click

213
00:09:07,166 --> 00:09:09,166
 on a clip selects only the picture.

214
00:09:09,433 --> 00:09:10,833
 The sound stays behind.

215
00:09:11,166 --> 00:09:12,966
 Switch it back on, and picture and

216
00:09:12,966 --> 00:09:14,799
 sound are selected together again.

217
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:18,966
 The third button, link clips, actually
 splits them apart.

218
00:09:19,266 --> 00:09:21,066
 One press, and they're unlinked.

219
00:09:21,333 --> 00:09:24,466
 Now I can drag the sound on its own,
 away from the picture.

220
00:09:24,833 --> 00:09:28,333
 I'll put it back, select both, and
 press link clips again.

221
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:29,166
 Linked.

222
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:31,366
 But link clips can do more than that.

223
00:09:31,566 --> 00:09:34,266
 Select two separate clips, for example a

224
00:09:34,266 --> 00:09:37,466
 clip and a piece of music,
 and press link clips.

225
00:09:37,666 --> 00:09:39,266
 Now they are linked together.

226
00:09:39,533 --> 00:09:41,766
 Click one, and the other one
 is selected too.

227
00:09:42,133 --> 00:09:43,833
 Move it, and they move together.

228
00:09:44,133 --> 00:09:45,299
 So that's the difference.

229
00:09:45,399 --> 00:09:47,633
 Link decides how you select, and

230
00:09:47,633 --> 00:09:50,166
 link clips really ties clips together.

231
00:09:50,433 --> 00:09:51,266
 I'll undo that.

232
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:53,833
 Top right is new compound clip.

233
00:09:54,066 --> 00:09:56,600
 It turns the selected clips
 into one clip.

234
00:09:56,899 --> 00:09:58,533
 Create, and there it is.

235
00:09:58,566 --> 00:10:01,000
 One compound clip, with that little icon.

236
00:10:01,266 --> 00:10:03,366
 Great to keep a busy timeline tidy.

237
00:10:03,666 --> 00:10:06,333
 I'll undo it, because I still want
 to work on this clip.

238
00:10:06,666 --> 00:10:07,633
 Now the music.

239
00:10:07,899 --> 00:10:09,466
 Middle row, first button.

240
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:10,966
 Normalize audio.

241
00:10:11,299 --> 00:10:13,100
 Pick your level, and normalize.

242
00:10:13,266 --> 00:10:14,200
 Look at the waveform.

243
00:10:14,433 --> 00:10:16,399
 The music now has a steady level.

244
00:10:16,700 --> 00:10:18,366
 Next to it is auto align.

245
00:10:18,633 --> 00:10:20,533
 It lines up clips by their sound.

246
00:10:20,766 --> 00:10:23,600
 That's for when you film the same
 moment with two cameras.

247
00:10:23,633 --> 00:10:24,899
 Like the speeches at a wedding.

248
00:10:25,233 --> 00:10:28,166
 My city clips don't have that, so
 there's nothing to see here.

249
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:29,933
 The third and fourth button on the

250
00:10:29,933 --> 00:10:32,466
 middle row are mark in, and mark out.

251
00:10:32,733 --> 00:10:34,033
 Now I have a range.

252
00:10:34,299 --> 00:10:36,633
 Bottom row, third button, loop.

253
00:10:36,933 --> 00:10:40,700
 When I play now, it keeps playing
 that range, over and over.

254
00:10:40,899 --> 00:10:42,633
 Stop, and loop off again.

255
00:10:42,966 --> 00:10:46,766
 On the third clip, bottom row, first
 button, match frame.

256
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,633
 It opens the original file
 at exactly this

257
00:10:49,633 --> 00:10:52,166
 frame, so you can grab more
 of the same shot.

258
00:10:52,399 --> 00:10:53,566
 And back to the timeline.

259
00:10:53,899 --> 00:10:57,733
 The button next to it, Cinema Viewer,
 shows your film full screen.

260
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,299
 Escape takes you back.

261
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:02,899
 On this page, the dials can give
 you six more colors.

262
00:11:03,033 --> 00:11:04,833
 The dials have their own pages too.

263
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:08,133
 Swipe down on the dials, and these
 six colors appear.

264
00:11:08,399 --> 00:11:12,266
 From the top left down, apricot,
 blue, lime.

265
00:11:12,566 --> 00:11:15,700
 And on the right, brown,
 pink, and purple.

266
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,000
 Round button four gives you
 edit page three.

267
00:11:23,299 --> 00:11:25,033
 Remember the gaps from page one?

268
00:11:25,433 --> 00:11:27,466
 Here's how to close them all at once.

269
00:11:27,633 --> 00:11:30,100
 The music runs underneath
 though, and DaVinci

270
00:11:30,133 --> 00:11:33,233
 only closes a gap when it's
 empty on every track.

271
00:11:33,433 --> 00:11:35,333
 So, I click this little button on

272
00:11:35,333 --> 00:11:37,533
 the music track to leave the music out.

273
00:11:37,799 --> 00:11:40,533
 Then, top right, delete gaps.

274
00:11:40,666 --> 00:11:43,100
 Every gap is closed, in one press.

275
00:11:43,333 --> 00:11:46,266
 The last two buttons on the
 middle row swap clips.

276
00:11:46,399 --> 00:11:48,966
 Swap left swaps the selected
 clip with the

277
00:11:48,966 --> 00:11:52,000
 one on its left, and swap
 right moves it back.

278
00:11:52,299 --> 00:11:54,333
 Top left is Enable Clip.

279
00:11:54,533 --> 00:11:57,033
 It switches a clip off without
 deleting it.

280
00:11:57,333 --> 00:11:58,866
 Press it again, and it's back.

281
00:11:59,200 --> 00:11:59,966
 Now a new one.

282
00:12:00,266 --> 00:12:02,766
 I put the playhead in the middle
 of the third clip.

283
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,566
 Top row, second button.

284
00:12:04,833 --> 00:12:05,733
 Freeze frame.

285
00:12:05,966 --> 00:12:08,000
 The picture freezes, right here.

286
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:11,100
 When I play it, the rest of the
 clip just stands still.

287
00:12:11,266 --> 00:12:14,666
 Press freeze frame again, and the clip
 plays at normal speed again.

288
00:12:15,033 --> 00:12:17,266
 I switch the music track back
 on, and put the

289
00:12:17,266 --> 00:12:20,266
 playhead right on the cut between
 two sound clips.

290
00:12:20,433 --> 00:12:22,066
 Middle row, second button.

291
00:12:22,266 --> 00:12:23,100
 Crossfade.

292
00:12:23,333 --> 00:12:25,266
 One press, and the sound now fades

293
00:12:25,266 --> 00:12:27,633
 smoothly from one clip into the next.

294
00:12:27,866 --> 00:12:30,533
 The third button on the top
 row is title safe.

295
00:12:30,666 --> 00:12:32,200
 It shows the line where your text

296
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:34,466
 is always visible on every screen.

297
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:36,200
 Press it again, and it's gone.

298
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:38,133
 Middle row, first button.

299
00:12:38,266 --> 00:12:41,666
 Find Clip shows the selected clip
 in your media pool.

300
00:12:41,899 --> 00:12:43,533
 Bottom row, first button.

301
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:46,399
 Find Timeline does the same
 for your timeline.

302
00:12:46,666 --> 00:12:49,966
 The second button is New Timeline,
 which we used at the start.

303
00:12:50,233 --> 00:12:51,133
 And the colors?

304
00:12:51,233 --> 00:12:55,000
 On this page, swipe down on the
 dials twice for six more.

305
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:58,733
 That's 15 colors in total, all
 just one press away.

306
00:12:58,966 --> 00:13:03,833
 Olive, teal, navy, violet,
 tan, and beige.

307
00:13:04,066 --> 00:13:07,266
 And the third button on the bottom
 row, Duplicate Timeline.

308
00:13:07,533 --> 00:13:09,600
 It makes a copy of your timeline,
 so you can

309
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:11,866
 try something new without
 risking your edit.

310
00:13:12,100 --> 00:13:13,500
 I'll keep working in the copy.

311
00:13:17,766 --> 00:13:21,766
 Now the square buttons next to the
 wheel, and the FN button.

312
00:13:22,233 --> 00:13:25,433
 Back on edit page one, I'll
 fix one thing first.

313
00:13:25,666 --> 00:13:28,066
 The music is much longer than the film.

314
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:30,600
 I select it, put the playhead at the

315
00:13:30,666 --> 00:13:33,466
 end of the last clip, and use Trim End.

316
00:13:33,866 --> 00:13:35,833
 Now the music stops with the film.

317
00:13:36,299 --> 00:13:39,299
 The FN button changes what
 the other buttons do.

318
00:13:39,633 --> 00:13:41,600
 You hold it, and press another button.

319
00:13:41,966 --> 00:13:43,799
 Say I want to get rid of this clip.

320
00:13:44,166 --> 00:13:46,266
 Hold FN and press B.

321
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:47,399
 Ripple Delete.

322
00:13:47,733 --> 00:13:50,033
 The clip is gone, and the gap is closed.

323
00:13:50,399 --> 00:13:51,200
 Change my mind?

324
00:13:51,566 --> 00:13:53,666
 The Undo button brings it right back.

325
00:13:54,033 --> 00:13:55,866
 Next to undo is Save.

326
00:13:56,133 --> 00:14:00,033
 Your project is saved, and the word
 edited at the top disappears.

327
00:14:00,366 --> 00:14:02,766
 A and B move the selected clip.

328
00:14:03,133 --> 00:14:06,200
 A moves it up a track, and
 B moves it back down.

329
00:14:06,633 --> 00:14:09,333
 E is a right click, wherever
 your mouse is.

330
00:14:09,566 --> 00:14:10,299
 There's the menu.

331
00:14:10,633 --> 00:14:12,433
 And C and D you already know.

332
00:14:12,633 --> 00:14:14,666
 The start and the end of your timeline.

333
00:14:15,066 --> 00:14:18,466
 FN together with the round buttons
 opens your panels.

334
00:14:18,700 --> 00:14:21,133
 FN and 1, the media pool.

335
00:14:21,399 --> 00:14:22,700
 Off and on again.

336
00:14:23,033 --> 00:14:27,533
 FN and 2, the effects library, with
 your transitions and titles.

337
00:14:27,766 --> 00:14:31,833
 FN and 3, the inspector, with all
 the settings of your clip.

338
00:14:32,066 --> 00:14:34,166
 FN and 4, the mixer.

339
00:14:34,433 --> 00:14:37,000
 FN and 5, your power bins.

340
00:14:37,066 --> 00:14:38,166
 Off and on.

341
00:14:38,466 --> 00:14:42,366
 FN and 6, metadata, all the
 details of your clip.

342
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:47,299
 And FN and 7, the index, a list of
 every cut in your timeline.

343
00:14:47,666 --> 00:14:48,333
 One more.

344
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:50,933
 FN and C copies a clip.

345
00:14:51,233 --> 00:14:53,100
 I copy the first clip, select the

346
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:56,266
 second one, then hold FN and press A.

347
00:14:56,466 --> 00:14:57,700
 Paste attributes.

348
00:14:57,899 --> 00:14:59,833
 Here you choose what to copy over.

349
00:15:00,066 --> 00:15:01,733
 The clip color is ticked, so I

350
00:15:01,733 --> 00:15:04,233
 apply, and the second clip is orange too.

351
00:15:08,500 --> 00:15:09,833
 Hey, look at that!

352
00:15:10,133 --> 00:15:12,933
 Remember the break timer we started
 on the media page?

353
00:15:13,333 --> 00:15:16,133
 25 minutes have passed, and
 there's the reminder.

354
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:17,799
 It doesn't stop your work.

355
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,933
 It just lets you know it's a good
 moment for a short break.

356
00:15:21,233 --> 00:15:22,333
 So this is your cue.

357
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:26,133
 Grab a coffee, stretch your legs,
 and give your eyes a rest.

358
00:15:26,366 --> 00:15:28,566
 You'll come back with a fresh
 look at your edit.

359
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,733
 Stop timer, and let's get some
 color in this film.

360
00:15:36,033 --> 00:15:38,966
 Round button 5 takes us
 to the color page.

361
00:15:39,266 --> 00:15:40,700
 I start with the first clip.

362
00:15:40,966 --> 00:15:42,466
 Top left on the touchscreen.

363
00:15:42,899 --> 00:15:43,666
 Videoscopes.

364
00:15:44,066 --> 00:15:46,366
 Here you check your colors
 and your exposure.

365
00:15:46,933 --> 00:15:48,333
 Press it again to close them.

366
00:15:48,733 --> 00:15:51,966
 This clip is way too bright,
 so let's fix that.

367
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,899
 Middle row, first button.

368
00:15:54,233 --> 00:15:55,466
 Add serial node.

369
00:15:55,766 --> 00:15:57,333
 A fresh, empty node.

370
00:15:57,633 --> 00:16:00,166
 The three dials on the left
 work on that node.

371
00:16:00,399 --> 00:16:02,133
 These are studio only.

372
00:16:02,333 --> 00:16:04,533
 The top left dial is saturation.

373
00:16:04,833 --> 00:16:05,700
 More color.

374
00:16:05,899 --> 00:16:07,133
 See what happened to the node?

375
00:16:07,433 --> 00:16:08,966
 As soon as you turn one of these

376
00:16:08,966 --> 00:16:11,600
 dials, the node gets the
 name corrections.

377
00:16:11,666 --> 00:16:12,433
 Automatically.

378
00:16:12,633 --> 00:16:14,100
 You can't change that name.

379
00:16:14,366 --> 00:16:16,533
 That's the node where you
 do your saturation,

380
00:16:16,566 --> 00:16:19,399
 your midtones, and your highlights
 with the dials.

381
00:16:19,533 --> 00:16:22,933
 You can use them on other nodes too,
 but only on the corrections

382
00:16:22,933 --> 00:16:26,266
 node do you see DaVinci's own settings
 move along live.

383
00:16:26,533 --> 00:16:28,299
 The bottom left dial is gain.

384
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:30,033
 I bring the highlights down.

385
00:16:30,333 --> 00:16:32,899
 The middle one is gamma for the midtones.

386
00:16:33,066 --> 00:16:35,566
 Press one of these dials and
 it goes back to normal.

387
00:16:35,799 --> 00:16:37,799
 The button next to add serial node

388
00:16:37,833 --> 00:16:39,766
 adds a node before the current one.

389
00:16:40,033 --> 00:16:42,700
 The third button, label node,
 lets you give

390
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:45,500
 it a name so you always know
 what a node does.

391
00:16:45,633 --> 00:16:47,266
 Top row, last button.

392
00:16:47,533 --> 00:16:49,066
 Printer light hotkeys.

393
00:16:49,233 --> 00:16:51,133
 Press it once and the three dials on

394
00:16:51,133 --> 00:16:53,233
 the right become red, green, and blue.

395
00:16:53,666 --> 00:16:57,833
 A bit more red, a bit less blue,
 and a touch of green.

396
00:16:58,133 --> 00:16:59,233
 That's a warmer look.

397
00:16:59,433 --> 00:17:01,033
 Press the button again when you're done.

398
00:17:01,299 --> 00:17:02,966
 Middle row, last button.

399
00:17:03,233 --> 00:17:07,066
 Grab still saves this frame with
 its grade in your gallery.

400
00:17:07,266 --> 00:17:09,666
 The bottom row is all about comparing and

401
00:17:09,733 --> 00:17:12,400
 every one of these buttons
 works on and off.

402
00:17:12,566 --> 00:17:15,666
 Split original shows your grade
 next to the original.

403
00:17:15,933 --> 00:17:17,866
 Press it again and you're back to normal.

404
00:17:18,033 --> 00:17:20,133
 Split stills puts the still from your

405
00:17:20,133 --> 00:17:22,466
 gallery next to the clip and off again.

406
00:17:22,733 --> 00:17:25,233
 With two clips selected, split selected

407
00:17:25,233 --> 00:17:27,933
 shows them side by side to
 match your shots.

408
00:17:28,133 --> 00:17:28,733
 Off again.

409
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:32,799
 And split prev next shows the clip
 before and after this one.

410
00:17:33,099 --> 00:17:34,666
 Lost track of which split is on?

411
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:37,833
 Press the top right dial and you're
 always back to normal.

412
00:17:38,033 --> 00:17:39,633
 Top row, second button.

413
00:17:39,866 --> 00:17:40,833
 Light box.

414
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:42,633
 All your clips next to each other.

415
00:17:42,866 --> 00:17:43,566
 And off again.

416
00:17:43,833 --> 00:17:47,500
 Next to it is cinema viewer to judge
 your grade on the full screen.

417
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:50,933
 And finally, hold F, N and press D.

418
00:17:51,133 --> 00:17:52,799
 Bypass all grades.

419
00:17:52,900 --> 00:17:55,099
 That's the original and that's the grade.

420
00:17:55,266 --> 00:17:57,500
 The easiest before and after there is.

421
00:18:01,833 --> 00:18:05,433
 Round button 6 is the Fairlight
 page for your sound.

422
00:18:05,833 --> 00:18:07,799
 I select the second piece of music.

423
00:18:08,033 --> 00:18:09,633
 Middle row, first button.

424
00:18:09,933 --> 00:18:11,366
 Batch fade settings.

425
00:18:11,533 --> 00:18:13,400
 One and a half seconds to fade in,

426
00:18:13,666 --> 00:18:16,400
 two seconds to fade out and apply.

427
00:18:16,733 --> 00:18:19,133
 That piece now fades in and out.

428
00:18:19,366 --> 00:18:22,400
 The button next to it is
 apply batch fades.

429
00:18:22,599 --> 00:18:26,433
 I select the first piece of music,
 press it and it gets the same

430
00:18:26,433 --> 00:18:29,400
 fades in one go without opening
 that window.

431
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:31,966
 The middle left dial is track height.

432
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:34,633
 Keep your mouse over the
 tracks and turn it.

433
00:18:34,833 --> 00:18:36,466
 The bottom left dial makes the

434
00:18:36,466 --> 00:18:39,433
 waveforms bigger and pressing
 it puts them back.

435
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:42,566
 The bottom row works just like
 on the edit pages.

436
00:18:42,733 --> 00:18:46,033
 Mark in, mark out, loop and play.

437
00:18:46,266 --> 00:18:47,933
 Stop and loop off.

438
00:18:48,233 --> 00:18:50,433
 The dials on the right are
 the same as well.

439
00:18:50,566 --> 00:18:53,433
 Shuttle, fast shuttle and next clip.

440
00:18:57,700 --> 00:19:00,333
 Round button 7 is the Deliver page.

441
00:19:00,566 --> 00:19:03,000
 The film is done so let's export it.

442
00:19:03,333 --> 00:19:05,933
 The buttons on this page are studio only.

443
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:07,933
 Each one adds your timeline to the

444
00:19:07,933 --> 00:19:09,900
 render queue with the right settings.

445
00:19:10,266 --> 00:19:12,433
 YouTube, there it is in the queue.

446
00:19:13,066 --> 00:19:16,433
 Vimeo, TikTok and Instagram at 4x5.

447
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:18,500
 Middle row first button.

448
00:19:18,799 --> 00:19:23,333
 ProRes 422 HQ, a high quality
 master of your film.

449
00:19:23,666 --> 00:19:28,233
 The next three buttons are custom 1,
 2 and 3 for your own settings.

450
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:29,700
 Here's how you set one up.

451
00:19:29,966 --> 00:19:31,766
 Choose your settings, then open

452
00:19:31,766 --> 00:19:34,500
 this menu and pick save as new preset.

453
00:19:34,666 --> 00:19:38,000
 Give it a short name and end it with
 a hashtag and the number 1.

454
00:19:38,433 --> 00:19:40,966
 I'm calling mine client hashtag 1.

455
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,000
 Save.

456
00:19:42,366 --> 00:19:44,766
 Now press custom 1 and your timeline

457
00:19:44,766 --> 00:19:46,900
 goes into the queue with your own preset.

458
00:19:47,133 --> 00:19:48,200
 And look at your loop deck.

459
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,633
 The button now shows the name you chose.

460
00:19:50,833 --> 00:19:54,066
 Hashtag 2 and 3 work the same for
 the other two buttons.

461
00:19:54,299 --> 00:19:55,933
 Bottom row first button.

462
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:59,133
 Add to queue with whatever settings
 you have right now.

463
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:01,233
 Next to it, render all.

464
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:03,666
 DaVinci renders every job in the queue.

465
00:20:03,900 --> 00:20:07,900
 When I add one more job, render new
 renders only that new one.

466
00:20:08,066 --> 00:20:09,299
 The old ones are skipped.

467
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:11,833
 And if a render takes too
 long, bottom right.

468
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,033
 Stop render.

469
00:20:13,299 --> 00:20:16,333
 Swipe the touch screen to the right
 for three more buttons.

470
00:20:16,466 --> 00:20:18,966
 Thumbnail saves the current
 frame as a picture.

471
00:20:19,066 --> 00:20:20,733
 Perfect for your YouTube thumbnail.

472
00:20:21,066 --> 00:20:23,900
 Export folder opens the folder
 with your exports.

473
00:20:24,066 --> 00:20:24,799
 There they are.

474
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:27,299
 And clear render queue empties the queue.

475
00:20:27,633 --> 00:20:29,000
 The dials work here too.

476
00:20:29,233 --> 00:20:33,233
 Press the top left dial for mark in and
 the top right dial for mark

477
00:20:33,299 --> 00:20:35,566
 out to export just a part of your film.

478
00:20:35,833 --> 00:20:39,433
 In the free edition, the deliver page
 has quick export, add to

479
00:20:39,433 --> 00:20:43,166
 queue, render all, mark in,
 mark out and play.

480
00:20:47,433 --> 00:20:50,166
 Two more things for when your
 film is finished.

481
00:20:50,533 --> 00:20:52,666
 Back on the edit page, round button

482
00:20:52,666 --> 00:20:55,533
 8 on the bottom right, quick export.

483
00:20:55,900 --> 00:20:58,666
 Pick a format, click export
 and you're done.

484
00:20:59,133 --> 00:21:01,633
 And remember the bottom row
 of the media page?

485
00:21:01,766 --> 00:21:02,766
 Round button 1.

486
00:21:03,299 --> 00:21:06,433
 Timeline 9x16 makes a vertical copy of

487
00:21:06,433 --> 00:21:09,466
 your timeline for TikTok,
 Reels and Shorts.

488
00:21:09,733 --> 00:21:11,666
 On the edit page, there it is.

489
00:21:11,866 --> 00:21:14,166
 And your original stays just as it was.

490
00:21:14,500 --> 00:21:18,500
 Timeline 4x5 makes one for the Instagram
 feed, like this.

491
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,900
 And Timeline 4x3 makes a 4x3 version.

492
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:24,033
 All three are studio only.

493
00:21:24,566 --> 00:21:25,166
 And that's it.

494
00:21:25,533 --> 00:21:28,200
 One film, from the first
 import to the final

495
00:21:28,333 --> 00:21:31,700
 export, and every page and every
 button of the pack.

496
00:21:32,099 --> 00:21:35,533
 If a button ever does nothing, check
 that the keyboard shortcuts of

497
00:21:35,533 --> 00:21:39,099
 the pack are selected in DaVinci, under
 keyboard customization.

498
00:21:39,433 --> 00:21:43,200
 In the studio edition, also set external
 scripting to local.

499
00:21:43,633 --> 00:21:45,133
 Want to edit like this yourself?

500
00:21:45,366 --> 00:21:48,433
 The Tikka Studio's loop deck pack
 is in the description below.

501
00:21:48,666 --> 00:21:50,766
 Grab it, plug in your loop deck and make

502
00:21:50,766 --> 00:21:53,766
 your next edit a lot faster
 and a lot more fun.

503
00:21:54,099 --> 00:21:56,233
 Thanks for watching and see
 you in the next one.

